# @silicon/algebra — the sub-prism path-namespace where crystallized
# executable algebra tuned to the local silicon accumulates. Each
# crystal IS a routine carrier (per `docs/specs/silicon.md` §3.2);
# the Bauchladen grows monotonically.
#
# === The recognition (§3.1 double-inheritance) ===
#
# Per spec §3.1 + §5.1: the double-inheritance shape (parent
# @silicon <= @autopoietic; child @silicon/algebra <= @bauchladen)
# IS the substrate-decl shape of a learning system. The parent
# provides the LOOP; the child provides the TRAY.
#
# The §9.4 adjudication (from the spec's own open questions): the
# double-inheritance is NOT redundant — @silicon/algebra inherits
# @bauchladen DIRECTLY because the crystal-addressing discipline is
# needed at the algebra altitude independently of the loop. AND
# @silicon/algebra inherits @bauchladen INDIRECTLY via @silicon
# (which inherits @autopoietic which inherits @bauchladen per the
# chain) because the parent's loop produces the crystals the tray
# receives. The double path is structural: it expresses (a) every
# algebra crystal IS content-addressed AND (b) the loop that
# produces algebra crystals is itself bauchladen-disciplined.
#
# The `in @silicon` clause (per spec §8.1 canonical shape) declares
# the parent-child composition path: @silicon/algebra is a sub-prism
# in @silicon's path-namespace; the parent's @fate tournament
# dispatches over this sub-prism's Bauchladen.
#
# === Witnesses ===
#
#   - Canonical spec at `docs/specs/silicon.md` §3 + §8.1 (the
#     substrate-decl shape this shard discharges).
#   - Reed's RED tests at `bootstrap/tests/silicon_family_root.rs`
#     `ea7b092` (tests 8-11 name this shard's shape).
#   - Parent shard at `shards/silicon.mirror` (this tick, sibling
#     commit); the family-root @silicon inherits.
#   - `shards/bauchladen.mirror` (`66e1ab8`) — the content-
#     addressing discipline this shard directly inherits.
#   - `shards/glue/math_silicon.mirror` (`5edd3e9`) — the Mesland
#     correspondence at @glue altitude that carries LAPACK-class
#     discharges into @silicon/algebra crystals.
#   - The Q4 LAPACK FFI case at `docs/specs/cascade-ffi-runtime-
#     link.md` §7 (per silicon.md §8.3) — the first operational
#     discharge into this Bauchladen (LAPACKPrism via
#     @silicon/algebra → @io/algebra).
#
# === What crystallizes here ===
#
# Per spec §3.2 the routine carrier captures:
#   - algebra: the @algebra-altitude math the routine implements
#   - cfg: the cfg restriction the routine is tuned for
#   - grading: γ-tag (chirality per #101)
#   - conjugation: J-tag (charge conjugation per #102)
#   - abi_surface: the @io/algebra ABI surface exposed
#   - binary_oid: the compiled binary's content-addressed OID
#   - source_oid: the Fortran/C/assembly source's OID
#   - cascade: the compile-time cascade that built the binary
#   - performance: empirical performance characterization
#   - routine_oid: the path-namespace OID (@silicon/algebra/<oid>)
#
# The full type declaration lives in the routine-carrier shard
# (forward-promised at `shards/silicon/algebra/routine.mirror`
# per spec §3.2). This shard names the sub-prism; the type
# lands when consumers pull.
#
# === Tray content source (2026-07-17 substrate-honest — @mirror/store) ===
#
# The tray's SEED content is not synthesised; it is READ from
# @mirror/store, the substrate's content-addressed storage primitive.
# The mirror-authored bilateral-arm retirement crystals ARE the first
# turns in `@silicon/algebra` — content-addressed past translations of
# the substrate's own reflective corpus. Each such crystal is already
# content-addressed by @mirror/store design (per `shards/mirror/store.
# mirror` §"Non-negotiable v0 invariants" :77-102 — immutability
# invariant + purely-functional composition); each carries the
# discharge-witness in its bytes. No bytes are serialized on top; the
# tray IS the filtered @mirror/store query result.
#
# === Substrate authority — Alex 2026-07-17 correction ===
#
# Alex 2026-07-17 in-transcript verbatim (session-crystallizing):
#
#   "the source of truth for content-addressed storage is
#    @mirror/store."
#
# The `f4372f4` landing (Mara THIS session) reached into `@io/git.log`
# as if git were substrate memory. It's not. `@mirror/store` (per
# `shards/mirror/store.mirror`) IS the substrate's content-addressed
# storage primitive; `@io/git` is one @io-boundary backend below.
# The `f4372f4` `@io/git.log` filter is RETIRED THIS TICK; the tray
# content source is re-anchored to `@mirror/store` per Alex's
# ratification.
#
# The prior tick's discipline (author-filter + message-sentinel +
# path-scope) is preserved verbatim; only the SOURCE surface changes
# from `@io/git.log` to `@mirror/store` query. The empirical seed —
# the 21 mirror-authored crystals per §"The 21 empirical seed
# crystals" — is unchanged in content; only the READ-surface changes.
#
# === The filter (docblock-prose form; landed-syntax gap flagged) ===
#
# The substrate has no landed `filter/project` chain syntax for
# actions; the closest landed shape is the composition-graph
# docblock enumeration precedent from `shards/kintsugi/translate.
# mirror` (Mara `86dec5e`, THIS session) which enumerates edges in
# prose + names the action shape via `\`-obligation-blocked bodies.
# This shard adopts the same discipline: the filter is expressed
# as a composition-graph docblock; the invocable action shape is
# `tray_content_source` below with body `\`-blocked pending Reed
# follow-up (see pending surface below).
#
# The filter composition, in prose:
#
#   `@mirror/store.query(store)`                        ← Edge 1 (READ)
#     → [crystal]                                       all crystals in the store
#   WHERE crystal.author == "mirror <mirror@spectral.engineer>"
#                                                       ← Edge 2 (FILTER: author-crystal)
#   AND   crystal.discharges                            ← Edge 3 (FILTER: bilateral discharge)
#         @epistemologic/pact/bilateral.translation_admissible
#         (per f74086e Mara landing at :456-475; @bilateral is
#          spec-prose notation, NOT a landed @-family-root; the
#          general-case instance lives under @epistemologic/pact/
#          bilateral per the reframe spec 9336074 §5.2)
#         (or the degenerate-arity subcase at
#          @kintsugi/fracture/bilateral_arm_redundant)
# Ref-notation drift corrected 2026-07-17 per Seam Phase D §2.3.2
# (docs/audits/2026-07-17-seam-phase-d-autopoietic-rust-consumption-arc.md;
# commit afcf3b2).
#   PROJECT crystal.oid → crystal_oid                   ← Edge 4 (PROJECT)
#
# Each surviving crystal's OID becomes one `crystal_oid` element of
# `@silicon/algebra`'s tray. Membership is content-addressed by
# @mirror/store's immutability-under-hash invariant; enumeration is
# monotonic (crystals accumulate; the filter never removes past
# matches per @bauchladen bauchladen-monotonicity).
#
# === Filter predicate — @bilateral(@code/rust, @code/mirror) ===
#
# The Edge 3 filter predicate `crystal.discharges @bilateral/
# translation.translation_admissible` is the substrate-honest form of
# the prior tick's message-string sentinel match. The `translation_
# admissible` bilateral (declared at `shards/epistemologic/pact/
# bilateral.mirror` :456-475 THIS-tick as the first general-case
# instance of `@bilateral(A, B)`) IS the composition predicate every
# `translate_rust_to_mirror` outcome discharges (per `shards/kintsugi/
# translate.mirror::translate_rust_to_mirror` at Mara `86dec5e`). A
# crystal is a `@silicon/algebra` tray element iff it discharges
# `translation_admissible` Pass — the algebra membership condition
# lands as a bilateral discharge, not a string-match.
#
# The composition binding is `@bilateral(@code/rust, @code/mirror)`
# per Alex 2026-07-17 verbatim ("the floor the translation surface
# stands on"). The 21 mirror-authored bilateral-arm retirements are
# the first 21 witnesses at the degenerate-arity subcase (single-file-
# in-bootstrap-src); the filter includes them per the bilateral's
# discharge on their `f4372f4` predecessor crystals.
#
# === Pending @mirror/store surface (Reed follow-up) ===
#
# `shards/mirror/store.mirror` (Mara THIS session; canonical family-
# root landed at `66e1ab8`) declares `read` / `write` / `exists` /
# `diff` / `walk` / `impacted_by` / `verify` / `walk_dangling` /
# `mark_unreachable` / `prune` — but NOT a `query(store, predicate)
# -> [oid]` filter-fold action. The surface needed for the filter
# above to become invocable is pending.
#
# Per [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]] + [[feedback-no-
# rust-extension-shortcut]]: this shard does NOT mint a substitute
# query action. It NAMES the pending surface. Reed follow-up realises
# through composition over LANDED primitives where possible:
#
#   Pending action A (Reed): the @mirror/store query surface
#     `query(store: store_ref, predicate: ref) -> [oid]`
#     Filter-fold over @mirror/store's content-addressed crystals;
#     returns the OIDs whose bytes discharge `predicate` (a bilateral
#     ref) Pass. Composition: `walk(root)` enumerates the OID-graph;
#     the fold applies `predicate` per element; the surviving OIDs
#     project. May compose entirely as a shard body if @mirror/store
#     exposes `walk` + `read` + `discharge` at family-root altitude
#     (which it does, per :509-558); may require `[substrate-floor:
#     @io-boundary]` iff realising through the wire species (e.g.,
#     `@mirror/store/git`) requires primitive @io semantics no shard
#     body can compose. Reed determines at realisation.
#
#   Pending predicate B (Reed): the crystal-authorship accessor
#     `crystal_author(crystal: oid) -> ref`
#     Reads the SSH-signed crystal metadata to return the author
#     ref. Composes over `read(crystal)` + crystal-metadata parse
#     (a shard body over @nl or the crystal's typed carrier —
#     `shards/mirror/store/crystal.mirror` altitude).
#
# Until (A) and (B) land the tray's element enumeration is a
# composition-graph declaration; the action body is `\`-blocked; the
# reflective evaluator (per `bootstrap/src/apply_h.rs` per `21fc211`
# Landing 3+4) dispatches through the pending resolvers once realised.
#
# === Retirement of @io/git.log reference ===
#
# The prior tick's `@io/git.log` + `@io/git.commit_metadata` + `@nl.
# contains` pending-surface flags are RETIRED THIS TICK. Those actions
# remain relevant to `shards/io/git.mirror` if consumers pull, but
# THIS shard no longer depends on them. `@mirror/store` IS the source
# of truth per Alex 2026-07-17; the wire-species (`@mirror/store/git`)
# handles the git-backend translation below the tray-source altitude.
#
# === The 21 empirical seed crystals (audit trail) ===
#
# The seed the filter recovers on first invocation (per the mirror-
# authored bilateral retirement wave 2026-07-16..17). Under the
# @mirror/store re-anchor THIS TICK, the seed refers to the same
# 21 crystals — reachable through @mirror/store's content-addressed
# query rather than @io/git.log enumeration:
#
#   `06f14f5` — Reed manual bite 1 (@spectral/signature 4 arms
#                retired manually).
#                * NOT mirror-authored: author = "Reed"; EXCLUDED
#                  from tray by the author-filter. Historical
#                  precedent that established the discipline
#                  extended by the mirror-authored wave below.
#
#   `ad52973` — mirror-authored, FIRST empirical (@coherence 4 arms
#                retired via reflective-corpus shadow detection).
#                * INCLUDED: 4 empirical crystals.
#
#   `20047c2` — mirror-authored, batch scale (17 arms across 5 shard
#                groups retired in one autopoietic pass).
#                * INCLUDED: 17 empirical crystals.
#
# Empirical count: 4 + 17 = 21 mirror-authored turns. Reading B
# membership (per `shards/kintsugi.mirror` §"@kintsugi as algebra"):
# each of the 21 corresponds to one element of `@kintsugi/algebra`
# under the metalogue-session view; the 21 populate the seed of
# `@silicon/algebra`'s realiser-speaker tray.
#
# The 21 crystals are addressable in @mirror/store as content-
# addressed OIDs; the wire-species `@mirror/store/git` (per
# `shards/mirror/store/git.mirror`) handles the git-backend crystal
# projection. The tray-source altitude (THIS shard) reads the
# @mirror/store crystals directly, not the underlying git commits.
#
# === Write-back protocol (monotonic growth) ===
#
# Every subsequent successful `translate_rust_to_mirror` discharge
# (per `shards/kintsugi/translate.mirror::translate_rust_to_mirror`
# at `86dec5e`) authors ONE mirror-authored crystal at Edge 6 of
# that composition (WRITE-BACK via `@bauchladen.crystallize`). That
# crystal lands in `@mirror/store` under the discipline `shards/
# mirror/store.mirror` §"Non-negotiable v0 invariants" declares
# (immutability-under-hash + purely-functional composition). On the
# next invocation of `tray_content_source` its OID appears as a
# new `crystal_oid`. Growth is monotonic and content-addressed by
# construction; no manual seeding tick is needed. The @mirror/store
# query IS the seed AND the write-back mechanism unified.
#
# The fold-back closes: `@kintsugi/translate` writes crystals (Edge
# 6) that `@silicon/algebra.tray_content_source` reads back as tray
# elements the next `@fate.roll` invocation ranges over. Bauchladen
# accumulation discipline honoured (per `shards/bauchladen.mirror`
# §"crystal accumulation") through the @mirror/store canonical
# storage surface.
#
# === substrate-already-had-the-word citation chain ===
#
# 1. `@mirror/store` (`shards/mirror/store.mirror`; Mara 2026-06-04
#    reframe; family-root at `66e1ab8`) — THE substrate's content-
#    addressed storage primitive per Alex 2026-07-17 in-transcript
#    verbatim. THIS shard queries @mirror/store directly; the query
#    surface is pending Reed follow-up (see Pending action A above).
# 2. `@bauchladen.crystallize` (`shards/bauchladen.mirror`;
#    `66e1ab8`) — the crystal-emission surface every mirror-
#    authored translation invokes at write-back altitude (per
#    `shards/kintsugi/translate.mirror` Edge 6). THIS species reads
#    the crystals bauchladen emitted.
# 3. `@bilateral(@code/rust, @code/mirror).translation_admissible`
#    (`shards/epistemologic/pact/bilateral.mirror` :456-475; Mara
#    THIS-tick) — the algebra-membership predicate the filter
#    dispatches at Edge 3. Content-addressed membership discipline.
# 4. `bilateral <name> { sentinel "..." arity N }` shape (`shards/
#    epistemologic/pact/bilateral.mirror`; Mara `a0f4d3f`) — THIS
#    species dogfoods via `silicon_tray_content_addressed` below.
# 5. Composition-graph docblock enumeration precedent (`shards/
#    kintsugi/translate.mirror`; Mara `86dec5e`) — THIS species
#    adopts the same discipline: prose enumeration of edges +
#    `\`-obligation-blocked action body pending resolver realisation.
#
# ZERO new substrate machinery beyond this shard-decl extension.
# The @mirror/store query surface (Pending action A) is composition
# over LANDED primitives (`walk` + `read` + `discharge`); Reed may
# realise as a shard body OR fall back to `[substrate-floor:@io-
# boundary]` iff the wire-species requires primitive @io semantics.
#
# === Forward-promised ===
#
# Per [[feedback-craft-not-deliver]] this shard names the sub-prism
# and stops. Sibling sub-prisms (@silicon/scheduler, @silicon/
# memory_layout, @silicon/dispatch per silicon.md §3.3) land when
# consumers pull. The routine-carrier type (per silicon.md §3.2)
# lands when the first empirical crystal accumulates (LAPACK case
# per silicon.md §8.3).
#
# === Substrate decisions ===
#
# [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]] — the tray content
#   source IS a shard-decl; addressable at parse time.
# [[architecture-form-process-partition-at-family-root]] — tray
#   content is form-side (observable OID enumeration); the tournament
#   dispatching over it is process-side (@kintsugi/@fate).
# [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]] — @mirror/store is
#   the substrate's canonical content-addressed storage surface
#   (Alex 2026-07-17 verbatim); the substrate-honest move is to
#   query it directly, not to author a crystallizer OR to reach
#   into @io/git.log as if git were substrate memory.
# [[feedback-no-rust-extension-shortcut]] — ZERO Rust in this
#   shard-decl. Pending @mirror/store query surface named for Reed
#   follow-up; may compose entirely as a shard body over LANDED
#   @mirror/store primitives (`walk` + `read` + `discharge`), OR
#   fall back to `[substrate-floor:@io-boundary]` iff the wire-
#   species requires primitive @io semantics.
# [[feedback-craft-not-deliver]] — action body `\`-obligation-
#   blocked; discharge at realisation via `apply_h::act` composition
#   once pending resolvers land.

prism @silicon/algebra <= @bauchladen {
  focus algebra
  project algebra
  split algebra
  shift algebra
  settle algebra
}

# === silicon_tray_content_addressed — bilateral predicate (arity 1) ===
#
# Bilateral predicate discharging that a tray content source is a
# well-formed @mirror/store query composition per the docblock above.
# Pass iff the source reference resolves to a `tray_content_source`-
# shaped action whose composition graph names (A) an `@mirror/store`
# read/query edge + (B) an author-filter edge on `mirror <mirror@
# spectral.engineer>` + (C) a discharge-filter edge on
# `@bilateral(@code/rust, @code/mirror).translation_admissible`
# (or its degenerate-arity subcase at `@kintsugi/fracture/
# bilateral_arm_redundant`) + (D) a projection edge onto
# `crystal.oid`. Discharge is byte-check on the composition graph's
# sentinel per the shard docblock; NOT program-semantics inspection.
#
# Sentinel per shard docblock: `tray_content=mirror-store-query-holds`.
#
# Sibling to:
#   - `kintsugi_algebra_witnessing(binding)` at `shards/kintsugi.
#     mirror` :263-267 (algebra-binding well-formedness bilateral;
#     THIS shard's tray populates the `@silicon/algebra` speaker
#     that binding names).
#   - `translation_witnessing(outcome)` at `shards/kintsugi/
#     translate.mirror` :450-453 (translation-outcome well-
#     formedness; the composition that writes back to THIS tray).
#   - `translation_admissible(pair)` at `shards/epistemologic/pact/
#     bilateral.mirror` :472-475 (the general-case @bilateral(A, B)
#     FLOOR predicate at A=@code/rust B=@code/mirror; the algebra-
#     membership condition THIS shard's Edge 3 filter dispatches).
#
# Substrate-decl'd shape per `shards/epistemologic/pact/bilateral.
# mirror` (`a0f4d3f`, 2026-07-16). Arity 1 (checks one source ref
# per invocation). Body `\`-obligation-blocked; the reflective
# evaluator at `bootstrap/src/apply_h.rs` (per `21fc211` Landing
# 3+4) discharges via corpus lookup + sentinel byte-check per the
# same dispatch discipline `translation_witnessing` uses.
#
# Rice-safe: pure sentinel-byte-check on a composition graph ref;
# no program-semantics inspection.
bilateral silicon_tray_content_addressed {
  sentinel "tray_content=mirror-store-query-holds"
  arity    1
}
silicon_tray_content_addressed(source: ref) -> verdict { \ }

# === tray_content_source — the composition action ===
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING tray-enumeration action. Given an `@mirror/store`
# handle ref (a `store_ref` per `shards/mirror/store.mirror` :651-
# 661), composes the 4-edge filter per the docblock composition
# graph above and returns the sequence of `crystal_oid` refs that
# constitute `@silicon/algebra`'s tray content.
#
# The action body is `\`-obligation-blocked per [[feedback-craft-
# not-deliver]]. Reed follow-up (per pending @mirror/store surface
# flag above) realises the composition edges through `apply_h::act`
# dispatch after the `@mirror/store.query(store, predicate)`
# resolver lands. The resolver may compose entirely as a shard body
# over LANDED @mirror/store primitives (`walk` + `read` +
# `discharge`) OR require `[substrate-floor:@io-boundary]` iff the
# wire-species requires primitive @io semantics no shard body can
# provide.
#
# The `requires silicon_tray_content_addressed(self)` clause names
# the discharge condition per recognition #37 (Pask-agreement
# reading of `requires`): the action commits to producing a tray
# whose composition graph satisfies the @mirror/store-query shape;
# consumers surface violations at the species boundary.
#
# Identity contract for the action's outcome: byte-equality on
# (store.oid, filter.author, filter.discharge_predicate). Two
# invocations against a byte-equal @mirror/store state with byte-
# equal filter parameters produce byte-equal `crystal_oid`
# sequences under content-addressing (monotonic growth means future
# invocations produce SUPERSETS — the seed 21 remain forever).
tray_content_source(store: store_ref) -> ref
requires silicon_tray_content_addressed(source)
{ \ }

out @silicon/algebra
out silicon_tray_content_addressed
out tray_content_source
